<title>SWITZERLAND: U.S. drops panel request in EU grain dispute.</title>
<headline>U.S. drops panel request in EU grain dispute.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States on Wednesday withdrew a request for a World Trade Organisation (WTO) panel in its long-running dispute with the European union over grain tariffs.</p>
<p>The move came on the eve of the implementation of a reported agreement between the two covering key aspects of the dispute.</p>
<p>But neither trade power made any reference to the accord when the withdrawal of the request was announced by the chairman at a meeting of the WTO's Dispute Settlement Body.</p>
<p>The on-off row is focussed on an EU tariff system introduced in 1995 which Washington says violates agreements reached during world trade talks in 1993.</p>
<p>Last month the EU agreed to change its rice import system and open a new tariff quota for U.S. malting barley, two of the key products in the dispute, effective from May 1.</p>
<p>Geneva newsroom  + 41 22 733 38 31</p>
</text>
